  "s3": {
    "metadata": {
      "trials_per_point": 200,
      "n_w": 1,
      "d_ble": 100.0,
      "d_th": 100.0,
      "tau_rssi": -90.0,
      "baseline_delta_t_max_ms": 35.0,
      "notes": [
        "S3 evaluates prover-prover collusion by modeling the attack as relay-assisted challenge-response forwarding under the common d_ble, d_th, and RSSI thresholds, while scanning only delta_t_max to calibrate the timing trade-off.",
        "Honest RTT is modeled as BLE roundtrip plus signing time.",
        "Relay RTT adds extra relay-path delay, either BLE+BLE or BLE+WiFi/LTE.",
        "Honest prover positions are sampled within 5-19 m of the witness so that distance and RSSI plausibility remain consistent under the common thresholds."
      ]
    },
